  "content": "# Bounded LRU Cache in Python: A Complete Tutorial\n\nAn LRU (Least Recently Used) cache is a memory-efficient data structure that evicts the least recently used items when the cache reaches its capacity limit. It\u2019s widely used in databases, web caching layers, and operating systems for page replacement.\n\nPython\u2019s `collections.OrderedDict` provides an ordered dictionary that maintains insertion order. This makes it a natural choice for implementing an LRU cache, where \"most recently used\" items are moved to the end and \"least recently used\" items sit at the beginning.\n\n## Core Design\n\nThe LRU cache has two main operations:\n\n1. **`get(key)`**: Retrieve the value associated with `key`. If `key` doesn\u2019t exist, return a default value (typically `None`). A successful `get` marks the item as most recently used, moving it to the end of the internal order.\n\n2. **`put(key, value)`**: Insert or update the value for `key`. If the cache is at capacity and the key is new, evict the least recently used item (the first item in the ordered dictionary). Then insert or update the key at the end, marking it as most recently used.\n\nThe key insight is that `OrderedDict.move_to_end(key)` allows us to promote an existing key to the most-recently-used position in O(1) time.\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A bounded Least Recently Used (LRU) cache backed by collections.OrderedDict.\n    \n    The cache maintains a fixed capacity. When capacity is exceeded, the least\n    recently used entry is evicted. Both get() and put() operations run in O(1)\n    average time.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the LRU cache.\n\n        Args:\n            capacity: Maximum number of items the cache can hold. Must be >= 1.\n\n        Raises:\n            ValueError: If capacity is less than 1.\n        \"\"\"\n        if capacity < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cache capacity must be at least 1\")\n        self._capacity = capacity\n        self._store: OrderedDict[Any, Any] = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: Any, default: Any = None) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"",
